{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And they gave their hand</b> — an allusion to raising the hand in an oath, or giving the hand like a person who surrenders himself to another to do his will and his request. So too נתנו יד — we surrendered ourselves to them." "<b>And guilty</b> — an adjective of the noun. And he explained: and the guilty ones gave their hand to offer a ram of the flock, and we have not found a guilt-offering punishment for one who lies with a gentile woman, and perhaps this was the counsel of the leaders."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:26.148633364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}